// Round duct silencers (Rohrschalldämpfer): manufacturer tables, transcribed 1:1.
// Schema, units, conventions and known source quirks: docs/silencer-data.md.
// Audited 2026-10-14 against the owner's local manufacturer PDFs. Source quirks stay as printed.
//
// Row: { series, dn, dIn?, L, insulation, core, dOuter, de, dp, dpFromDn?, note? }
//   dn          nominal size = connection diameter [mm]; Schako dIn is the source's outside spigot diameter ød
//   L           nominal order length [mm]; not necessarily the overall or acoustic length
//   insulation  thickness of the absorber lining [mm]
//   core        width T of the splitter / middle baffle [mm], null = no core
//   dOuter      casing diameter [mm]
//   dOuterMax   maximum casing diameter including seams/ribs [mm], excluding optional accessories
//   bodyLength  casing/absorber length [mm]; Trox: acoustic L1; Schako: L; Lindab: l
//   overallLength overall standard product length [mm]; Schako KA0 includes two 50 mm spigots
//   de          insertion loss D_e [dB] for OCTAVES (63 ... 8000 Hz); 50 means 'at least 50' (manufacturer cap)
//   dp          depends on series.dpModel:
//                 'duct'           null, Δp like a straight duct of length L (λ from lib/core/air.js)
//                 'flow-points'    { q: volume flow [m³/h], pa: Δp_t [Pa] } measured points for this L
//                 'velocity-table' { v: velocity in the free cross-section [m/s], pa: Δp_t [Pa] }

